      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "El primero era Panaʻewa, el moʻo que mandaba en el bosque sobre Hilo.",
          "en": "The first was Panaʻewa, the moʻo who ruled the forest above Hilo."
        },
        {
          "es": "Podía ser lagarto, persona, niebla o lluvia. Y hacía perderse a los viajeros.",
          "en": "It could be a lizard, a person, fog or rain. And it made travelers lose their way."
        },
        {
          "es": "Dos pajaritos le servían de espías. «Es una de las mujeres del cráter», dijo uno.",
          "en": "Two little birds were its spies. \"She is one of the women from the crater,\" said one."
        },
        {
          "es": "«No es tan fuerte como Panaʻewa», dijo el otro. Hiʻiaka los oyó, y se rió.",
          "en": "\"She is not as strong as Panaʻewa,\" said the other. Hiʻiaka heard them, and laughed."
        }
      ],
