      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Agotada, Hiʻiaka llamó a su hermana: «¡Pele!».",
          "en": "Exhausted, Hiʻiaka called out to her sister: \"Pele!\""
        },
        {
          "es": "Desde Kīlauea, Pele la oyó. Y mandó tormentas de rayos contra el bosque.",
          "en": "From Kīlauea, Pele heard her. And she sent lightning storms against the forest."
        },
        {
          "es": "Una lluvia enorme llenó los barrancos de agua roja, y arrastró a los ayudantes de Panaʻewa hasta el mar.",
          "en": "A great rain filled the ravines with red water, and swept Panaʻewa's helpers down to the sea."
        },
        {
          "es": "El bosque quedó libre. Hasta hoy, esa tierra cerca de Hilo se llama Panaʻewa.",
          "en": "The forest was free. To this day, that land near Hilo is called Panaʻewa."
        }
      ],
