      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los moʻo batieron el agua en remolinos, para arrastrar a las viajeras al río.",
          "en": "The moʻo churned the water into whirlpools, to drag the travelers into the river."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hiʻiaka los golpeó con su falda, una y otra vez, con la fuerza del rayo.",
          "en": "Hiʻiaka struck them with her skirt, again and again, with the force of lightning."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los dos moʻo quedaron vencidos. Westervelt dice que se volvieron bloques de piedra.",
          "en": "Both moʻo were defeated. Westervelt says they turned into blocks of stone."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hiʻiaka le devolvió todo al jefe. «El camino ya es seguro para tu gente», le dijo.",
          "en": "Hiʻiaka gave the chief back everything. \"The way is safe for your people now,\" she said."
        },
        {
          "es": "¿Tú habrías apostado tu vida como Hiʻiaka?",
          "en": "Would you have bet your life like Hiʻiaka?"
        }
      ],
